    {
      "id": "be-s12m-monopoly-c1",
      "heading": "The monopoly environment and its sources",
      "explanation_md": "A **monopoly\\** is a **single firm serving the relevant market\\**. Most real monopolies are **local\\**: the only cinema in a small town.\n\nBecause it is the only seller, **its demand curve is the market demand curve\\**. It controls the price, but a higher price means it sells less.\n\nWhere does the power come from?",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Natural: scale, scope, cost complementarities. Created: patents and licenses, tying contracts, exclusive contracts.",
      "clarification": null,
