      "memory_trick": "**Monopoly: P > MC, so too few units, too high a price.**",
      "exam_answer_md": "Under monopoly **P > MC\\**: too little output at too high a price, creating a **deadweight loss\\**. No long-run adjustment occurs unless the source of monopoly power is eliminated.\n\n**Arguments for monopoly:** economies of scale, scope and cost complementarities may outweigh the negative effects of market power; it encourages innovation. **Multi-plant rule:** MR(Q) = MC1(Q1) = MC2(Q2), with P = P(Q), Q = Q1 + Q2. (Draw D, MR, MC and shade the deadweight-loss triangle.)"
    }
