      "id": "be-s12m-monopoly-q-9929a5de",
      "type": "long",
      "stem": "A monopolist faces P = 10 - Q and C(Q) = 6 + 2Q. Find the profit-maximizing output, price and profit, and explain why governments dislike monopoly.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "- MR = 10 - 2Q (MR = a - 2bQ) and MC = 2.\n- Set **MR = MC**: 10 - 2Q = 2, so **Q = 4**.\n- Price from demand: **P = 10 - 4 = $6**.\n- Profit = (6)(4) - (6 + 8) = **$10**.\n\nGovernments dislike monopoly because **P > MC**: output is too low and price too high, creating a **deadweight loss**.",
